{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible light-mediated oxidative decarboxylation of arylacetic acids bearing a para-amino group to generate benzyl radicals. These radicals undergo addition to electron-deficient alkenes using transition metal polypyridyl complexes (iridium and ruthenium) as photoredox catalysts, yielding benzylated products in good to high yields. The study highlights the necessity of the para-amino group for efficient decarboxylation and radical formation.",
